011, "y1": 0.13364413364413363}, {"text": "Write an essay in which you explore the interplay of the personal and the political in", "x0": 0.17472527472527472, "y0": 0.1445221445221445, "x1": 0.8285714285714286, "y1": 0.1585081585081585}, {"text": "After the Bomb.", "x0": 0.17472527472527472, "y0": 0.16938616938616938, "x1": 0.2978021978021978, "y1": 0.1794871794871795}, {"text": "In your response, refer to TWO prescribed texts AND texts of your own choosing.", "x0": 0.17472527472527472, "y0": 0.20901320901320902, "x1": 0.810989010989011, "y1": 0.222999222999223}, {"text": "Question 8 \u2014 Elective 1: After the Bomb (25 marks)", "x0": 0.17472527472527472, "y0": 0.27195027195027194, "x1": 0.6, "y1": 0.28438228438228436}, {"text": "Civilization is maintained by a very few people in a small number of places and we", "x0": 0.1989010989010989, "y0": 0.30303030303030304, "x1": 0.845054945054945, "y1": 0.317016317016317}, {"text": "need only some bombs and a few prisons fo blot it out altogether.", "x0": 0.3373626373626374, "y0": 0.31934731934731936, "x1": 0.843956043956044, "y1": 0.33255633255633255}, {"text": "Use all or part of the provided text in a piece of imaginative writing that reflects your", "x0": 0.17472527472527472, "y0": 0.3667443667443667, "x1": 0.8351648351648352, "y1": 0.37995337995337997}, {"text": "understanding of anxiety in After the Bomb.", "x0": 0.17472527472527472, "y0": 0.38306138306138304, "x1": 0.5153846153846153, "y1": 0.3954933954933955}, {"text": "Question 9 \u2014 Elective 2: Romanticism (25 marks)", "x0": 0.17472527472527472, "y0": 0.46231546231546233, "x1": 0.5802197802197803, "y1": 0.4755244755244755}, {"text": "Romantic writers were fired by ideas of personal and political liberty and of the", "x0": 0.17362637362637362, "y0": 0.49417249417249415, "x1": 0.7945054945054945, "y1": 0.5073815073815073}, {"text": "energy and sublimity of the natural world.", "x0": 0.17472527472527472, "y0": 0.5097125097125097, "x1": 0.4978021978021978, "y1": 0.5229215229215229}, {"text": "Write an essay in which you discuss this quotation. In your response, refer to TWO", "x0": 0.17472527472527472, "y0": 0.5415695415695416, "x1": 0.8186813186813187, "y1": 0.5547785547785548}, {"text": "prescribed texts AND texts of your own choosing.", "x0": 0.17362637362637362, "y0": 0.5571095571095571, "x1": 0.5604395604395604, "y1": 0.5703185703185704}, {"text": "Question 10 \u2014 Elective 2: Romanticism (25 marks)", "x0": 0.17472527472527472, "y0": 0.6363636363636364, "x1": 0.5725274725274725, "y1": 0.6487956487956488}, {"text": "\"Musing in Solitude, I oft perceive", "x0": 0.17472527472527472, "y0": 0.682983682983683, "x1": 0.43626373626373627, "y1": 0.6961926961926962}, {"text": "Fair trains of imagery before me rise,", "x0": 0.17472527472527472, "y0": 0.6993006993006993, "x1": 0.4593406593406593, "y1": 0.7117327117327117}, {"text": "Accompanied by feelings of delight", "x0": 0.17362637362637362, "y0": 0.714063714063714, "x1": 0.44945054945054946, "y1": 0.728049728049728}, {"text": "Pure, or with no unpleasing sadness mixed\u201d", "x0": 0.17362637362637362, "y0": 0.7303807303807304, "x1": 0.510989010989011, "y1": 0.7435897435897436}, {"text": "William Wordsworth", "x0": 0.17362637362637362, "y0": 0.7622377622377622, "x1": 0.3362637362637363, "y1": 0.7723387723387724}, {"text": "Use all or part of the quotation in a piece of imaginative writing that reflects your", "x0": 0.17472527472527472, "y0": 0.8096348096348096, "x1": 0.8043956043956044, "y1": 0.8228438228438228}, {"text": "understanding of Romanticism.", "x0": 0.17362637362637362, "y0": 0.8259518259518259, "x1": 0.4142857142857143, "y1": 0.8391608391608392}], [{"text": "In your answers you will be assessed on how well you:", "x0": 0.16373626373626374, "y0": 0.12198912198912198, "x1": 0.589010989010989, "y1": 0.1351981351981352}, {"text": "\u00a2 demonstrate understanding of how particular ways of thinking have shaped", "x0": 0.16483516483516483, "y0": 0.1383061383061383, "x1": 0.7692307692307693, "y1": 0.1522921522921523}, {"text": "and are reflected in texts", "x0": 0.189010989010989, "y0": 0.15462315462315462, "x1": 0.378021978021978, "y1": 0.16472416472416473}, {"text": "an extended composition appropriate to the question, demonstrating", "x0": 0.24615384615384617, "y0": 0.17094017094017094, "x1": 0.7714285714285715, "y1": 0.18492618492618493}, {"text": "control in the use of language", "x0": 0.189010989010989, "y0": 0.18725718725718726, "x1": 0.4175824175824176, "y1": 0.20046620046620048}, {"text": "Question 11 \u2014 Elective 3: Navigating the Global (25 marks)", "x0": 0.16483516483516483, "y0": 0.2556332556332556, "x1": 0.654945054945055, "y1": 0.26961926961926963}, {"text": "Write an essay in which you explore the interplay of choice and in", "x0": 0.16373626373626374, "y0": 0.28826728826728826, "x1": 0.7868131868131868, "y1": 0.3014763014763015}, {"text": "Navigating the Global.", "x0": 0.16483516483516483, "y0": 0.3038073038073038, "x1": 0.34065934065934067, "y1": 0.317016317016317}, {"text": "In your response, refer to TWO prescribed texts AND texts of your own choosing.", "x0": 0.16483516483516483, "y0": 0.3356643356643357, "x1": 0.8021978021978022, "y1": 0.34887334887334887}, {"text": "Question 12 \u2014 Elective 3: Navigating the Global (25 marks)", "x0": 0.16483516483516483, "y0": 0.39937839937839936, "x1": 0.6604395604395604, "y1": 0.4125874125874126}, {"text": "When we first met,", "x0": 0.4164835164835165, "y0": 0.432012432012432, "x1": 0.5648351648351648, "y1": 0.44366744366744365}, {"text": "you were living", "x0": 0.421978021978022, "y0": 0.44755244755244755, "x1": 0.5439560439560439, "y1": 0.46076146076146074}, {"text": "in that stone house.", "x0": 0.42637362637362636, "y0": 0.46386946386946387, "x1": 0.5736263736263736, "y1": 0.473970473970474}, {"text": "Salt air, strong winds", "x0": 0.4186813186813187, "y0": 0.49572649572649574, "x1": 0.5824175824175825, "y1": 0.5081585081585082}, {"text": "You stood afraid of nothing", "x0": 0.4142857142857143, "y0": 0.5112665112665112, "x1": 0.6285714285714286, "y1": 0.5244755244755245}, {"text": "Reproduced with the kind permission of", "x0": 0.5747252747252747, "y0": 0.5454545454545454, "x1": 0.8351648351648352, "y1": 0.5563325563325563}, {"text": "Jill Chan", "x0": 0.7043956043956044, "y0": 0.5617715617715617, "x1": 0.7615384615384615, "y1": 0.5703185703185704}, {"text": "\u2018Use all or part of the provided text in a piece of imaginative writing that reflects your", "x0": 0.16483516483516483, "y0": 0.6068376068376068, "x1": 0.8252747252747252, "y1": 0.6208236208236209}, {"text": "understanding of changing realities in Navigating the Global.", "x0": 0.16483516483516483, "y0": 0.6231546231546231, "x1": 0.6384615384615384, "y1": 0.6363636363636364}], [{"text": "Module C: Language and Values", "x0": 0.1901098901098901, "y0": 0.1111111111111111, "x1": 0.5065934065934066, "y1": 0.1258741258741259}, {"text": "50 marks", "x0": 0.1912087912087912, "y0": 0.12975912975912976, "x1": 0.2802197802197802, "y1": 0.1414141414141414}, {"text": "You must attempt TWO questions from the elective you have studied", "x0": 0.1912087912087912, "y0": 0.16472416472416473, "x1": 0.7615384615384615, "y1": 0.17793317793317792}, {"text": "Allow about J hour for each question", "x0": 0.1912087912087912, "y0": 0.19658119658119658, "x1": 0.4956043956043956, "y1": 0.2097902097902098}, {"text": "Answer each question in a SEPARATE writing booklet.", "x0": 0.1912087912087912, "y0": 0.22843822843822845, "x1": 0.6516483516483517, "y1": 0.24164724164724163}, {"text": "In your answers you will be assessed dn how well you:", "x0": 0.19230769230769232, "y0": 0.2595182595182595, "x1": 0.6164835164835165, "y1": 0.27350427350427353}, {"text": "\u00a9 understanding of the ways in which language shapes and reflects,", "x0": 0.19230769230769232, "y0": 0.2766122766122766, "x1": 0.8153846153846154, "y1": 0.289044289044289}, {"text": "culture and values", "x0": 0.2153846153846154, "y0": 0.29292929292929293, "x1": 0.35604395604395606, "y1": 0.30225330225330227}, {"text": "\u00a9 sustain an extended composition appropriate to the question, demonstrating", "x0": 0.19230769230769232, "y0": 0.30924630924630925, "x1": 0.798901098901099, "y1": 0.32245532245532244}, {"text": "control in the use of language", "x0": 0.2153846153846154, "y0": 0.3247863247863248, "x1": 0.44395604395604393, "y1": 0.337995337995338}, {"text": "The electives for this module are:", "x0": 0.1912087912087912, "y0": 0.38461538461538464, "x1": 0.46483516483516485, "y1": 0.3947163947163947}, {"text": "+ Elective 1: Textual Dynamics \u2014 Attempt Questions 13 and 14 (page 13)", "x0": 0.19230769230769232, "y0": 0.43045843045843046, "x1": 0.7923076923076923, "y1": 0.44366744366744365}, {"text": "The prescribed texts are:", "x0": 0.19230769230769232, "y0": 0.4630924630924631, "x1": 0.3813186813186813, "y1": 0.47707847707847706}, {"text": "+ Prose Fiction \u2014 John Fowles, The French Lieutenant's Woman", "x0": 0.19230769230769232, "y0": 0.49417249417249415, "x1": 0.6945054945054945, "y1": 0.5058275058275058}, {"text": "~ Italo Calvino, If on a winter's night a traveller", "x0": 0.3131868131868132, "y0": 0.5097125097125097, "x1": 0.689010989010989, "y1": 0.5353535353535354}, {"text": "\u2014Robert Dessaix, Night Letters", "x0": 0.3131868131868132, "y0": 0.5415695415695416, "x1": 0.5571428571428572, "y1": 0.554001554001554}, {"text": "+ Film Potter, Orlando", "x0": 0.1934065934065934, "y0": 0.6045066045066045, "x1": 0.4945054945054945, "y1": 0.6161616161616161}, {"text": "+ Elective 2: Language and Gender \u2014 Attempt Questions 15 and 16 (page 13)", "x0": 0.1934065934065934, "y0": 0.6666666666666666, "x1": 0.8274725274725274, "y1": 0.6806526806526807}, {"text": "The prescribed texts are:", "x0": 0.1978021978021978, "y0": 0.6993006993006993, "x1": 0.3868131868131868, "y1": 0.7125097125097125}, {"text": "+ Prose Fiction - Virginia Woolf, Orlando", "x0": 0.25164835164835164, "y0": 0.7148407148407149, "x1": 0.6318681318681318, "y1": 0.7272727272727273}, {"text": "+ Drama ~ William Shakespeare, Twelfth Night", "x0": 0.25164835164835164, "y0": 0.7381507381507382, "x1": 0.6681318681318681, "y1": 0.7513597513597513}, {"text": "+ Poetry John Tranter, The Floor of Heaven", "x0": 0.25164835164835164, "y0": 0.7622377622377622, "x1": 0.6527472527472528, "y1": 0.7746697746697747}, {"text": "+ Film ~Shekhar Kapur, Elizabeth", "x0": 0.25164835164835164, "y0": 0.7855477855477856, "x1": 0.5659340659340659, "y1": 0.7987567987567987}, {"text": "il", "x0": 0.5197802197802198, "y0": 0.9184149184149184, "x1": 0.5362637362637362, "y1": 0.9277389277389277}], [{"text": "In your answers you will be assessed on how well you:", "x0": 0.16923076923076924, "y0": 0.11888111888111888, "x1": 0.5934065934065934, "y1": 0.1320901320901321}, {"text": "\u00a9 demonstrate understanding of the ways in which language shapes and reflects", "x0": 0.17032967032967034, "y0": 0.1351981351981352, "x1": 0.7912087912087912, "y1": 0.14840714840714841}, {"text": "culture and values", "x0": 0.1934065934065934, "y0": 0.15151515151515152, "x1": 0.33406593406593404, "y1": 0.16161616161616163}, {"text": "\u2018sustain an extended composition appropriate to the question, demonstrating", "x0": 0.16923076923076924, "y0": 0.16783216783216784, "x1": 0.7747252747252747, "y1": 0.18181818181818182}, {"text": "control in the use of language", "x0": 0.19230769230769232, "y0": 0.18414918414918416, "x1": 0.421978021978022, "y1": 0.19658119658119658}, {"text": "Question\u2019 13 \u2014 Elective 1: Textual Dynamics (25 marks)", "x0": 0.16923076923076924, "y0": 0.23076923076923078, "x1": 0.6065934065934065, "y1": 0.24475524475524477}, {"text": "\u2018Write an essay in which you explore the interplay of insight and transformation in Textual", "x0": 0.16813186813186815, "y0": 0.2641802641802642, "x1": 0.8362637362637363, "y1": 0.2773892773892774}, {"text": "Dynamics.", "x0": 0.16813186813186815, "y0": 0.2804972804972805, "x1": 0.24615384615384617, "y1": 0.29215229215229216}, {"text": "In your response, refer to TWO prescribed texts AND texts of your own choosing.", "x0": 0.16813186813186815, "y0": 0.31002331002331, "x1": 0.7769230769230769, "y1": 0.3247863247863248}, {"text": "Question 14 \u2014 Elective 1: Textual Dynamics (25 marks)", "x0": 0.17362637362637362, "y0": 0.3434343434343434, "x1": 0.610989010989011, "y1": 0.35664335664335667}, {"text": "Alll the Christmases roll down toward the two-tongued sea, like a cold and headlong moon", "x0": 0.16813186813186815, "y0": 0.3752913752913753, "x1": 0.8362637362637363, "y1": 0.3885003885003885}, {"text": "bundling down the sky that was our street; and they stop at the rim of the ice-edged fish-", "x0": 0.16813186813186815, "y0": 0.3916083916083916, "x1": 0.823076923076923, "y1": 0.4048174048174048}, {"text": "freezing waves, and I plunge my hands in the snow and bring out whatever I can find, In", "x0": 0.16813186813186815, "y0": 0.40792540792540793, "x1": 0.8219780219780219, "y1": 0.4219114219114219}, {"text": "goes my hand into that wool-whitebell-tongued ball of holidays resting at the rim of the", "x0": 0.16813186813186815, "y0": 0.4234654234654235, "x1": 0.8164835164835165, "y1": 0.4366744366744367}, {"text": "carol-singing sea, and out come Mrs. Prothero and the firemen.", "x0": 0.16813186813186815, "y0": 0.4397824397824398, "x1": 0.6362637362637362, "y1": 0.4522144522144522}, {"text": "\u00a9 Dylan Thomas", "x0": 0.6912087912087912, "y0": 0.4553224553224553, "x1": 0.8164835164835165, "y1": 0.4677544677544678}, {"text": "Use all or part of the provided text in a piece of imaginative writing that reflects your", "x0": 0.16813186813186815, "y0": 0.48562548562548563, "x1": 0.798901098901099, "y1": 0.4988344988344988}, {"text": "understanding of playfulness in Textual Dynamics.", "x0": 0.16813186813186815, "y0": 0.5019425019425019, "x1": 0.545054945054945, "y1": 0.5143745143745144}, {"text": "Question 15 \u2014 Elective 2: Language and Gender (25 marks)", "x0": 0.16813186813186815, "y0": 0.5493395493395493, "x1": 0.6395604395604395, "y1": 0.5625485625485626}, {"text": "Write an essay in which you explore the interplay of identity and concealment in", "x0": 0.16813186813186815, "y0": 0.5811965811965812, "x1": 0.765934065934066, "y1": 0.5951825951825952}, {"text": "Language and Gender.", "x0": 0.16703296703296702, "y0": 0.5975135975135976, "x1": 0.33516483516483514, "y1": 0.6107226107226107}, {"text": "In your response, refer to TWO prescribed texts AND texts of your own choosing.", "x0": 0.16813186813186815, "y0": 0.6293706293706294, "x1": 0.7769230769230769, "y1": 0.6425796425796426}, {"text": "Question 16 \u2014 Elective 2: Language and Gender (25 marks)", "x0": 0.16813186813186815, "y0": 0.6612276612276612, "x1": 0.6604395604395604, "y1": 0.6744366744366744}, {"text": "This language is a borrowed dress", "x0": 0.2835164835164835, "y0": 0.6775446775446775, "x1": 0.5472527472527473, "y1": 0.6899766899766899}, {"text": "I put on", "x0": 0.2835164835164835, "y0": 0.6938616938616938, "x1": 0.34285714285714286, "y1": 0.7062937062937062}, {"text": "but never truly wear.", "x0": 0.2835164835164835, "y0": 0.7094017094017094, "x1": 0.44285714285714284, "y1": 0.7218337218337219}, {"text": "It is functional enough:", "x0": 0.2835164835164835, "y0": 0.7249417249417249, "x1": 0.46153846153846156, "y1": 0.7389277389277389}, {"text": "hides what must be hidden,", "x0": 0.2835164835164835, "y0": 0.7412587412587412, "x1": 0.49340659340659343, "y1": 0.7536907536907537}, {"text": "enables me to blend into streets and supermarket aisles", "x0": 0.2835164835164835, "y0": 0.7575757575757576, "x1": 0.7076923076923077, "y1": 0.7707847707847708}, {"text": "Reproduced with the", "x0": 0.5736263736263736, "y0": 0.7762237762237763, "x1": 0.7076923076923077, "y1": 0.7871017871017871}, {"text": "Kind permission of Amelia Walker", "x0": 0.5747252747252747, "y0": 0.7917637917637917, "x1": 0.8, "y1": 0.8034188034188035